From 9af967e38e2fcee556681efcb4d1f42bfa85d743 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:08:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(multiaxis): start and exit picks for the 5-axis
 parallel

A start pick chooses the raster corner where the cut starts (an end of
the first or the last pass); an exit pick chooses where the last pass
ends. The passes keep their geometry; only their order and direction
change, before the raster's own link laws plan the links. A pick far
from every corner, and an exit that the start's order cannot end at,
are refused by name. No pick keeps the automatic raster byte for byte.

Refs #3330

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
